mmary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.8.dev (46173009d)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev (46173009d) - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors (3840x2160 @ 120.00 Hz, 3840x2160 @ 60.00 Hz) - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9186) - AMD Ryzen 7 7800X3D 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 63.11 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\n`ItemList` has extra space next to it when no scrollbar is visible, similar to when using `SCROLL_MODE_RESERVE` in a `ScrollContainer`. I think `ItemList` would benefit from options like `ScrollMode` in `ScrollContainer` to control scrollbar behavior.\n\n### With Scrollbar\n<img width=\"372\" height=\"189\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/98cf42ee-f412-4d10-899c-ec8b70e800dc\" />\n\n### Without Scrollbar\n<img width=\"384\" height=\"218\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/411f9c5d-14b1-4b71-8cc9-e0439cc54388\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Find an `ItemList` in the editor with clickable elements (`History`, `FileSystem` in split mode, `Donors` (only affects first link), ...)\n- Hover over the elements while the scrollbar is/isn't visible\n- In both cases the same area will be highlighted, the items don't grow when the scrollbar isn't visible\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"TheDying0fLight","id":95179191,"node_id":"U_kgDOBaxRtw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95179191?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight","html_url":"https://github.com/TheDying0fLight","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/following{/other_user}","gists